<p class="lt-chem-36442">Using the knowledge of the electron donating or withdrawing effects of subsituents gained in Section 16.6, rank the following compound in order of decreasing basicity.</p>

<ol start="1" style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
    <li class="lt-chem-36442"><em>p</em>-Nitroaniline, methyl p-aminobenzoate, <em>p</em>-chloroaniline</li>
    <li class="lt-chem-36442"><em>p</em>-Bromoaniline, <em>p</em>-Aminobenzonitrile, <em>p</em>-ethylaniline</li>
    <li class="lt-chem-36442">p-(Trifluoromethyl)aniline, <em>p</em>-methoxyaniline, <em>p</em>-methylaniline</li>
</ol>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answers</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <ol start="1" style="list-style-type: lower-alpha;">
        <li class="lt-chem-36442"><em>p</em>-Chloroaniline, methyl p-aminobenzoate, <em>p</em>-nitroaniline</li>
        <li class="lt-chem-36442"><em>p</em>-Ethylaniline, <em>p</em>-Bromoaniline, <em>p</em>-aminobenzonitrile</li>
        <li class="lt-chem-36442"><em>p</em>-Methoxyaniline, <em>p</em>-methylaniline, <em>p</em>-(trifluoromethyl)aniline</li>
    </ol>
    </dd>
</dl>
